every finite\ntype point of <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0016> be a <MATH_0017>-morphism of categories\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0018>. We say <MATH_0019> satisfies\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>openness of versality<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if given a scheme <MATH_0020> locally of finite type\nover <MATH_0021>, an object <MATH_0022> of <MATH_0023> over <MATH_0024>, openness\nof versality holds for\n<MATH_0025>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e07c25d147183c84cf6024605a6d58a09edc19345d2856ef29a6306359a10e83", "unit_id": "tag:07XQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "artin", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "07XP", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9e470b8fe5dae10793df181aff9ab751e810d7dc0bbcea96baf18d2425d116f5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOpenness of versality is often the hardest to check. The following example\nshows that requiring this is necessary however.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:18de168574903a15871339965b4c9376dbbc747bd7d213b26f2c317c549a1571", "unit_id": "tag:07XP:prose-0002"}
